        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          Expedition 74 began on December 9, 2025, at 01:41 UTC, with the undocking of Soyuz MS-27 from the International Space Station (ISS). The departing crew included Sergey Ryzhikov (RSA), Alexey Zubritsky (RSA), and Jonny Kim (NASA), concluding their mission and marking the end of Expedition 73.<div><br></div><div>Remaining aboard and transitioning to Expedition 74 were Commander Mike Fincke (NASA) and Flight Engineers Zena Cardman (NASA), Oleg Platonov (RSA), Kimiya Yui (JAXA), Sergey Kud-Sverchkov (RSA), Sergey Mikaev (RSA), and Chris Williams (NASA). The Expedition 74 crew continued station operations, supported ongoing scientific investigations, and prepared for upcoming visiting vehicle traffic and extravehicular activities.</div><div><br></div><div>On January 7, 2026 a medical incident occurred aboard the ISS. Using their extensive training and preparation for such contingencies, fellow crew members and ground teams responded to the incident. A statement by NASA indicated that the affected crew member was in stable condition. </div><div><br></div><div>In consultation with flight surgeons, and in the interest of ensuring crew safety, the agency elected to bring Crew-11 home early to enable the continued post-incident medical workup of the affected crew member on the ground using capabilities that are not currently available on the ISS.</div><div><br></div><div>On January 14, 2026 at 22:15 UTC, Crew Dragon <i>Endeavor</i> undocked from the Node 2 Zenith Port of the ISS and began its journey back to Earth. The capsule splashed down in the Pacific Ocean off the coast of California on January 15, 2026 at 08:41 UTC, safely transporting NASA astronauts Zena Cardman and Mike Fincke, JAXA astronaut Kimiya Yui and Roscosmos cosmonaut Oleg Platonov home. </div><div><br></div><div>Following the landing, the crew was taken to a local area hospital to facilitate a medical evaluation of the crew member that experienced the medical incident. After an overnight stay, the crew continued on to Houston.</div><div><br></div><div>February at the station saw the arrival of Crew 12. Crew 12 launched from Space Launch Complex 40 at the Cape Canaveral Space Force Station in Florida on February 13, 2026 at 10:15 UTC. Crew Dragon <i>Freedom </i>is commanded by Jessica Meir (NASA), piloted by Jack Hathaway (NASA), and includes mission specialists Sophie Adenot (ESA) and Andrey Fedyaev (RSA). The crew dragon arrived at the station and docked to the Node 2 Zenith port on February 14, 2026 at 20:15 UTC. The arrival of Crew 12 marked the return of the station to it's nominal seven member crew compliment. </div><div><br></div><div>Expedition 74 is expected to conclude in July of 2026 with the departure of Soyuz MS-28. This record will be updated as mission operations unfold.</div><div><br></div><div>Last updated [2026-03-10]</div>
        </div>

